PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
  • Data: web reads `useVehicles()[0]` as a sample then queries
    `/analytics/anomalies?vehicle_id={id}&days=1`; native binds the same two hooks via
    the P1/S8 `AnomalyInlineRowSource` seam (production wraps the shared useVehicles +
    useAnomalies holders) — no HTTP in the view.
  • Status: web SEVERITY_TO_STATUS (critical->unhealthy, warning->degraded,
    info->unknown) reproduced + unit-asserted.
  • Summary: web `${count} in 24h · ${signal} ${formatRelative(detected_at)}` ported
    verbatim; formatRelative s/m/h/d ladder + the non-finite "recently" branch ported
    + unit-asserted (en_US golden values).
  • The web component renders NOTHING when there are 0 anomalies in 24h. The Apple
    surface contract requires every state to render (never a blank box), so the dormant
    case becomes a calm healthy-tinted "No anomalies in the last 24h" row. The exact web
    null decision is preserved + unit-tested as `webRendersRow(_:)` so the two never
    drift (documented enhancement, NOT silent drift).
  • Navigation: web `to="/anomaly-detection"`. There is no native AppRoute case for it,
    so the row emits the canonical path through `AnomalyInlineRowDestination` +
    the model's activation seam; the host maps it. The view never navigates itself.
  • Charts/maps: NONE in the web source — nothing to port to Swift Charts / MapKit.

